  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reaching out. Your laptop is online, and your account is active with VPN access turned on. The Duo prompt is showing up because Duo was never set up for your account, so the VPN can't finish signing you in yet. This is normal for a new laptop. To finish setup, we need about 10 to 15 minutes with you and your work phone. We'll install Duo Mobile on your phone, set up the Duo app on your laptop, and send a test approval request. Please reply with a few times this week that work for you, and make sure your phone is with you. Until this is done, VPN won't connect, so please don't keep retrying the sign-in. Also, your account is flagged to change your password at next sign-in, so have that ready when we connect.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for user_id 12 (Hannah Lee, Finance, Payroll Specialist, not VIP, America/New_York, 09:00-17:00). Account active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, failed_login_count 0, must_change_password true, password last set 2026-10-11. check_mfa_status: enrolled false, so Duo was never set up. This matches KB-004 (not enrolled, laptop issued without Duo). check_device_status on BL-LT-0112 (Windows 11 Pro, assigned to Hannah): online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:45 UTC, 130 GB free, no warnings. Nothing was changed. Next step: schedule a remote or in-person Duo enrollment session with the user present with her phone. Install Duo Mobile, install the Duo client on BL-LT-0112 if missing, scan the activation QR, and send a test push. Note for the user: VPN stays blocked until enrollment is done. Not a security issue, since no sign-in blocks and no failed attempts. I did not check sign-in logs because the cause is already clear. Could not schedule the session with my tools.",
